#Ac 2:16-18|

    16-18. Peter continues:

    (16) But this is that which was spoken through the prophet Joel;

#Ac 2:26|

    (26) Therefore did my heart rejoice, and my tongue was glad.
 Moreover, my flesh shall rest in hope;

#Ac 3:7|

    (7) And seizing him by the right hand, he lifted him up, and 
 immediately his feet and ankles received strength;

#Ac 3:14|

    (14) But you rejected the holy and just, and desired a murderer to
 be granted to you;

#Ac 5:35|

    (35) And he said to them, Men of Israel, take heed to yourselves
 what you are about to do respecting these men;

#Ac 6:13|

    (13) and set up false witnesses, who said, This man ceases not to
 speak blasphemous words against this holy place and the law;

#Ac 10:37|

    (37) the word which was published throughout all Judea, beginning
 from Galilee after the immersion which John preached,

#Ac 13:23|

    (23) From this man&amp;apos;s offspring God has, according to his promise,
 raised up to Israel a Saviour, Jesus;

#Ac 13:36|

    (36) For David, after he had served his own generation by the will
 of God, fell asleep, and was added to his fathers, and saw corruption;

#Ac 14:6|

    (6) they, being aware of it, fled down to the cities of Lycaonia,
 Lystra, and Derbe, and the surrounding country;

#Ac 14:16|

    (16) who in generations past suffered all the Gentiles to go on in
 their own ways;

#Ac 15:19|

    (19) Therefore, my judgment is, not to trouble those of the Gentiles
 who turn to God;

#Ac 16:23|

    (23) And having laid many stripes upon them, they cast them into
 prison, charging the jailer to keep them safely;

#Ac 20:19|

    (19) serving the Lord with all humility and many tears and trials
 which befell me by the plots of the Jews;

#Ac 20:26|

    (26) Wherefore, I call you to witness this day, that I am pure from 
 the blood of all;

#Ac 22:4|

    (4) I persecuted this way, even to death; binding and delivering
 into prisons both men and women;

#Ac 26:6|

    (6) Even now, it is for the hope of the promise made by God to the
 fathers, that I stand here to be judged;

#Ac 28:19|

    (19) But the Jews opposing it, I was compelled to appeal to Caesar; 
 not that I had any thing of which to accuse my nation.

#Ac 28:26|

    (26) saying, Go to this people and say, With hearing you will hear
 and will not understand, and seeing, you will see and not perceive;

